  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Prolonged period of dry and quiet \nweather with moderating temperatures next week leading to \nincreasingly mild afternoons with cool nights.\n\nSunshine should be more abundant today compared to yesterday as we \nare increasingly removed from the mid level trough, though its \neffects will linger. We'll continue to see diurnal clouds pop up and \nwe'll have efficient mixing up to near 800mb. This will pull down \nsome breezy NW gusts, generally 20-25 mph. Combined with highs in \nthe upper 40s it will feel closer to the low to mid 40s for most, \nmid 30s in the slopes of the Berkshires. \n\nThere is good consensus amongst the guidance that this coming week \nwill be dominated by a very broad surface high pressure/mid level \nridging pattern with troughing over the intermountain west. Rising \nheights will lead to warming temperatures and keep skies mostly \nsunny, especially Tuesday and beyond. Dry NW flow around the high \nwill lead to chilly low temperatures exacerbated at times by \nradiational cooling while highs warm well above average, into the \n60s by mid to late week. Eventually a dry cold front cools the \nairmass down just a bit late week but no arctic intrusions on \nthe horizon. Overall a fantastic stretch of weather for late \nNovember if you're looking to get outside and enjoy some \nrelatively warmer days.",
